      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand what needs to be improved.Now I understand the test. I'll improve it by:\n1. Giving descriptive names to variables\n2. Adding a clear test method name\n3. Making the intent of calling `toString()` twice explicit (it tests the caching behavior of the CUT)The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored version uses descriptive variable names (`threeSecondsAfterEpoch`, `utcInstant`, `formattedInstant`), a self-documenting method name, and a comment that explains *why* `toString()` is called twice — to exercise both the cache-miss and cache-hit paths of the CUT's racy single-check caching idiom."
